# UI Title Case

S2F Race Day Timing uses **Title Case** for titles, buttons, tabs, and major links — not sentence case.

## Apply Title Case to

- Window / page titles (`StepTitle`, window `Title`)
- Buttons (`Content=…`)
- Admin tabs and header links (`Admin`, `Setup New Event`, …)
- Primary list-row choices that act like actions (`One Race`, `Templates Folder`)
- Dialog primary/secondary action buttons

## Do not Title-Case

- Body copy, subtitles, breadcrumbs that are instructional sentences, status lines, tooltips, error messages
- Field helper text under inputs
- File/path names and product strings that must match disk (`RUNSCORE`, `.event`)

## Conventions

- Capitalize principal words; keep short closed-class words lowercase unless first/last: *a, an, the, and, or, but, for, to, of, in, on, with*
- Verb particles in labels are capitalized: **Sign In**, **Sign Out**, **Check for Updates**
- Keep product/proper nouns as branded: OneDrive, RunScore, Timing & Scoring, Past Races, Admin
- Prefer **Setup** (not “Set Up”) in short tab/button labels already used in this app

## Examples

| Avoid (sentence case) | Use (Title Case) |
| --- | --- |
| Create event | Create Event |
| Choose another event | Choose Another Event |
| Refresh events | Refresh Events |
| Browse race files | Browse Race Files |
| Sign in to OneDrive | Sign In to OneDrive |
| Admin settings | Admin Settings |
| Choose your office | Choose Your Office |
